<newsitem itemid="548859" id="root" date="1997-04-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: Allied Properties 1996 net flat.</title>
<headline>Allied Properties 1996 net flat.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   10.5	 vs 10.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0	  vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  26.70 gain vs 16.84 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    253.67     vs 253.27</p>
<p>    Turnover		     309.04     vs 469.47</p>
<p>    Company name		 Allied Properties (Hong Kong) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 16-20</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Allied Properties, a subsidiary of Allied Group Ltd, is a property investment and development company.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 2000 warrant for five shares held. Each warrant will entitle its holder to subscribe for one fully paid ordinary share at an initial subscription price of HK$1.50 and is exercisable at any time from the start of dealing in the warrants on the stock exchange (expected to be July 4, 1997) until July 3, 2000.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of interest in an unlisted associated company.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is one H.K. cent vs two cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
